     iiccoonnvv --ll

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiccoonnvv utility converts the codeset of _f_i_l_e (or from standard input if
     no file is specified) from codeset _f_r_o_m___n_a_m_e to codeset _t_o___n_a_m_e and out‐
     puts the converted text on standard output.

     The following options are available:

     --cc    Prevent output of any invalid characters.  By default, iiccoonnvv out‐
           puts an “invalid character” specified by the _t_o___n_a_m_e codeset when
           it encounts a character which is valid in the _f_r_o_m___n_a_m_e codeset but
           does not have a corresponding character in the _t_o___n_a_m_e codeset.

     --ff    Specifies the source codeset name as _f_r_o_m___n_a_m_e.

     --ll    Lists available codeset names.  Note that not all combinations of
           _f_r_o_m___n_a_m_e and _t_o___n_a_m_e are valid.

     --ss    Silent.  By default, iiccoonnvv outputs the number of “invalid
           characters” to standard error if they exist.  This option prevents
           this behaviour.

     --tt    Specifies the destination codeset name as _t_o___n_a_m_e.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The iiccoonnvv utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Convert _f_i_l_e_._t_x_t from IBM273 to UTF-8 and save the result to
     _c_o_n_v_e_r_t_e_d_._t_x_t:

           iconv -f IBM273 -t UTF-8 file.txt > converted.txt

